  "summary_en": "US Coast Guard regulation (33 CFR Part 104) setting maritime security requirements for vessels: security officers, vessel security assessments and plans, MARSEC levels, access control with TWIC, drills, records and audits. It has no AI or robotics content beyond brief provisions on unmanned vessels/barges.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Applies to SOLAS vessels, large cargo vessels, passenger vessels, barges, tankships and towing vessels.",
   "Owners must designate a Company Security Officer and Vessel Security Officer.",
   "Vessel Security Assessment and Vessel Security Plan must be approved by the Marine Safety Center, valid 5 years, and audited annually.",
   "Security measures scale across MARSEC Levels 1-3, including TWIC-based access control.",
   "Unmanned vessels have special VSO and documentation rules."
